<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  A WRAPPED TAKE COLUMN MUST PLAY THE ACTIVE TAKE THROUGH THE TAKE'S OWN
  WINDOW. This is an AUDIO gate, and the defect it holds shut was audible.

  THE SHAPE. A take column reaches a track two ways: DIRECT
  (`SLink -> STakeStack`, what add-take builds) and WRAPPED
  (`SLink -> SCut -> STakeStack`, what a SHARED or PLACED column is - the
  stack carries nRefs > 1 and each placement is its own SCut window into it).
  Only the wrapped shape goes through a CAPTURE, and only the wrapped shape
  was broken: on the direct shape a take slip has always been audible, which
  take_lane_slip.qxa gates.

  THE DEFECT. SCut::buildCapture_'s container branch rendered
  `content->getRootComponent()` from position 0, and that dropped the
  content's own window TWO independent ways:

    * getRootComponent() returns the built READER when one exists and falls
      back to the raw, UNWINDOWED content when it does not. At capture-build
      time the inner take's reader typically does not exist yet - and the
      capture is CACHED, so it latched on first use.
    * Even WITH the reader built it was still wrong: a plain reader is
      addressed in the WARPED domain with the slip folded in BY THE CALLER
      (SCut::clipToReaderMap), and freezing from 0 applies no mapping at all.

  So the take's srcStart was lost either way - and because the wrapper's
  PLAYBACK reader is built over that same capture, the clip PLAYED the wrong
  part of the take. It is now resolved through SObject::resolveClip(), the
  same authority twView asks on the playback path, which yields the component
  and the mapping from ONE snapshot (proposal 19 Inv-1).

  THE FIXTURE IS A CLOSED FORM, not a measurement. takestack_wrap_takeslip.qxp
  puts a 2 s wrapper window 2 s into the stack (srcStart='96000'), and the
  active take is itself slipped half a second in (srcStart='24000'), over
  test_gapsaw.wav - a 0.1 -> 0.8 amplitude ramp with EXACT-ZERO regions at
  [0.6,0.9) and [2.5,3.0) s. So the clip must play source [2.5, 4.5) s:

      clip 0.0-0.5 s  -> source [2.5,3.0)  -> the SILENCE
      clip 0.5-1.5 s  -> source [3.0,4.0)  -> the ramp's loud tail
      clip 1.5-2.0 s  -> past the 4 s file -> SILENCE

  A sawtooth of amplitude A has RMS A/sqrt(3), and the ramp is linear, so the
  two loud windows have closed forms 0.38610 and 0.43662. Measured on the
  first run: 0.38640 and 0.43689 - four decimal places, no fitting.

  WHY THE FIRST AND LAST WINDOWS ARE THE GATE. Unwindowed, the clip would play
  source [2.0, 4.0) instead: the silence would land at clip 0.5-1.0 s and BOTH
  the first and the last window would be loud. So silent-loud-loud-silent
  against loud-silent-loud-loud discriminates the two readings at every one of
  the four windows, and the two ends flip outright.

  NOT asserted here: the drawn composite lane. A container-backed clip only
  previews once its capture is reachable, which is a separate fix on its own
  branch (fix/take-lane-capture-align); this case deliberately measures the
  AUDIO, which is where the defect actually bit.
-->
<SActionScript version="1" name="wrapped_take_window">

  <setup project="new"/>

  <actions>
    <load-project path="../takestack_wrap_takeslip.qxp"/>

    <render filename="wrapped_take_window.wav" format="wav" quality="10"
            durationSec="2.0"/>

    <!-- clip 0.0-0.5 s = the source's [2.5,3.0) SILENCE. Unwindowed this
         window is source [2.0,2.5) and reads RMS 0.285. -->
    <assert-audio-energy filename="wrapped_take_window.wav"
                         startFrame="0" frameCount="24000"
                         minRms="0.0" maxRms="0.002"/>

    <!-- clip 0.5-1.5 s = source [3.0,4.0), the ramp's loud tail. Closed form
         A/sqrt(3) over each half: 0.38610 and 0.43662. -->
    <assert-audio-energy filename="wrapped_take_window.wav"
                         startFrame="24000" frameCount="24000"
                         minRms="0.380" maxRms="0.392"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="wrapped_take_window.wav"
                         startFrame="48000" frameCount="24000"
                         minRms="0.430" maxRms="0.443"/>

    <!-- clip 1.5-2.0 s = past the end of the 4 s file. Unwindowed this window
         is source [3.5,4.0) and reads RMS 0.487. -->
    <assert-audio-energy filename="wrapped_take_window.wav"
                         startFrame="72000" frameCount="24000"
                         minRms="0.0" maxRms="0.002"/>
  </actions>

</SActionScript>
